**Finding: deviation (INDEMN — critical)**

Section 12(b) contains a TrueLink indemnity, but it is confined to TrueLink's breach of the Agreement or failure to perform. It omits:
- any duty to **defend**;
- **third-party IP infringement** claims relating to the Interface/Hosting/Support Services (no such indemnity or warranty exists anywhere — §2(a) and §8(b) only address Client-side infringement risk);
- TrueLink's **breach of law**, **unauthorised access/disclosure of our data**, and **gross negligence/wilful misconduct**;
- any indemnification procedure.

By contrast, our indemnity in 12(a) is broad (including strict-liability style product/service claims under 12(a)(iv)).

Redline validated (ok:true) and submitted: adds "defend" to 12(b) and expands it into limbs (i)–(v) covering IP infringement, breach of law, data breach caused by TrueLink and gross negligence/wilful misconduct, plus a standard notice/control/cooperation mechanic. Fallback offered in the comment: customary IP indemnity exclusions (Client modifications, combinations, specifications) and procure/modify/replace/refund remedies. Note the §12 indemnity is not caught by the liability cap in p0077 (which covers only Sections 3, 4, 7 and 11), so no super-cap carve-out was needed.
